# Auto commit and push

After finishing a task that changes tracked files in this repository:

1. Commit the changes without asking the user for confirmation.
2. Push to the tracked remote branch (usually `origin/master`) without asking.
3. Do not ask "should I commit?" or "should I push?" — just do it.

Follow the git safety protocol: no force push to main/master, no amending pushed commits, no skipping hooks unless the user explicitly requests it.

If commit or push fails, fix the issue and retry; report the final commit hash and remote status briefly.
